  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"All reasonable out-of-pocket business expenses\" is undefined and measured only against the Corporation's own \"standard policies,\" which are not attached or described. Reasonableness has no benchmark in the Agreement.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.12}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The clause declares Executive an at-will employee terminable \"for any reason or no reason ... at any time,\" then in the same sentence entitles him to \"ninety (90) days prior notice\" if terminated without Cause. Whether the ninety-day notice is a condition of termination, a payment obligation, or defeated by the at-will language is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44},
    {"issue": "The clause twice refers to the termination date \"specified in accordance with this Section 4,\" but the notice provisions are in Section 5 and Section 4 is Compensation and Benefits. The mis-numbered self-reference makes the operative mechanism uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
