  {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The defined \"Business\" is an enumerated list of software and IT services closed by no catch-all, so whether the Corporation's other lines of activity fall inside \"Business\" (and thus inside the non-compete's \"Competitive Enterprise\") is open. The list's scope drives the reach of every restrictive covenant.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c014", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This warranty that Executive is \"not a party to any restrictive covenant\" duplicates and is narrower than Section 7(ii), which warrants he is bound by no employment, non-compete or confidentiality agreement. Which representation controls if they diverge is not addressed.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.10}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The prohibition on engaging in \"any new transactions, deals or relations of any kind including but not limited to\" the listed activities is a catch-all far broader than the enumerated specifics that follow, and \"inconsistent, or incompatible with interests or obligations of the Corporation\" has no ascertainable boundary. The clause's actual reach can only be settled by construction.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.45},
    {"issue": "The restriction runs \"During the Term of this Agreement and for a period of twenty-four (24) months after termination,\" but \"Term\" is a capitalized term that is defined nowhere in the Agreement, and no Section 9 definition supplies it. It is also unclear whether \"termination of this Agreement\" means termination of employment.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c016", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The parenthetical says \"capitalized terms used but not defined herein are defined below,\" yet \"Competitive Enterprise\" is defined above in the Conflict of Interest paragraph and \"Affiliate\" is defined both below in Section 6 and again in Section 9(a). Which definitions this covenant borrows must be worked out from the instrument as a whole.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c017", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Solicit\" is defined to include communication \"regardless of by whom initiated\" and any \"advising, encouraging or requesting\" of any person to take or refrain from any action, which sweeps in responses to unsolicited approaches and ordinary conversation. The term has no workable limit as drafted.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c018", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Client\" is defined circularly (\"means any customer, Client or prospective client\") and extends to any prospective client \"whose identity became known to the Executive,\" a category with no boundary. What counts as a protected Client is therefore indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c019", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This Section 6 definition of \"Affiliate\" (ten percent ownership or control of any Person) conflicts with Section 9(a), which defines \"Affiliate\" for purposes of the whole Agreement as an entity controlling, controlled by or under common control with the Corporation. Two different meanings are available for the same capitalized term used in the same covenants.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33},
    {"issue": "The definition includes \"members of the Family of such Person,\" but \"Family\" is capitalized and defined nowhere in the Agreement. Its scope is left entirely open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c020", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This Section 6 definition of \"Person\" sits alongside the Section 12(e) definition of \"person,\" which enumerates a different list (including groups, syndicates, cooperatives and governmental bodies). Which list governs the capitalized \"Person\" used in the Affiliate definition is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.17}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c021", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"The abovementioned provision\" is singular and unidentified: it may refer only to the Non-Solicitation of Clients covenant, or to the Conflict of Interest covenant, or to all of the preceding covenants. The breach that triggers this damages remedy cannot be fixed from the words used.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c022", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The carve-out \"unless prior written consent is given by the Executive\" makes the Executive the consenting party to his own prohibited hiring, which is a manifest drafting error for the Corporation. Read literally the covenant is self-defeating.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.40},
    {"issue": "The $50,000-per-employee \"fixed damages\" cannot be squared with the Remedies paragraph of Section 6, which entitles the Corporation to recover all profits and \"any damages suffered by the Corporation\" for breach of any covenant. Whether the liquidated sum is exclusive or cumulative is left open.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.26}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c023", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Confidential Information\" is defined as all information \"belonging to, used by, or in the possession of the Corporation\" across an open list \"of every kind and character,\" with only public-domain carve-outs, and the use/disclosure ban runs \"at any time\" without limit. The category has no ascertainable outer boundary.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.25}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c024", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The definitions of \"Assigned Inventions\" and \"Retained Inventions\" overlap and are set out in a sentence with unbalanced parentheses, so it is unclear whether an Invention conceived by Executive outside his employee capacity is assigned or retained. The grammar of the parenthetical changes which category prevails.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
    {"issue": "The carve-out for \"the materials listed on Exhibit B attached hereto\" refers to an exhibit the Agreement does not contain — only Exhibit A is attached and incorporated by Section 3. What, if anything, is carved out of the assignment cannot be determined from the instrument.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.26}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c025", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The duty to keep records of \"all inventions\" is in lower case and untied to the defined \"Invention,\" while the ownership sentence speaks of \"Assigned Inventions other than Retained Inventions\" even though Retained Inventions are by definition not assigned. Whether records of Retained Inventions must be kept and surrendered is left uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c026", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The power-of-attorney sentence is triggered \"[i]f the Corporation is unable because of the Corporation's mental or physical incapacity ... to secure the Corporation's signature,\" when the intended subject in each instance is the Executive. As written the condition can never occur for a corporate entity.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.38}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c027", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The NDA is executed \"[s]imultaneously herewith\" but is not attached or described, and Section 14 declares this Agreement the exclusive understanding superseding any \"contemporaneous agreement.\" Whether the NDA survives the integration clause — and it must, since Section 9(b) makes breach of the NDA a Cause event — requires reading the two together.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c028", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"The duration of every restriction set forth in this section will be extended by any period during which the Executive is in breach of his obligations\" is an open-ended tolling term with no cap, and \"this section\" is not identified (Section 6 contains many separately headed covenants). The extended duration of the covenants cannot be computed from the text.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c029", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Intentionally disparage\" and \"any public statement reflecting negatively\" are undefined and expressly extend \"irrespective of the truthfulness\" of the statement, with no time limit on the obligation. What speech is forbidden, and for how long, is left to construction.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c030", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The savings sentence preserves \"any other provision of this letter,\" although the instrument is an Agreement and not a letter, leaving the object of the severance clause misdescribed. The mismatch invites argument about what document the reformation provision operates on.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c031", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Excusing the Corporation from \"paying or performing any liability or obligation owed to the Executive (including compensation)\" on any breach of any covenant cannot be squared with Section 4, which makes salary and bonus payable as consideration for services rendered. The two provisions give opposite answers on forfeiture of earned compensation.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.29},
    {"issue": "The clause creates rights in a \"Third Party Beneficiary\" defined by reference to the Section entitled \"Third Party Enforcement; Assignment; Successors,\" but Section 10 addresses only assignment and identifies no third-party beneficiary other than an assignee. Who may enforce the covenants must be pieced together from the two provisions.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.21}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c032", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The representation that Executive is bound by no \"confidentiality agreement with any other person or entity\" overlaps the narrower warranty in the \"Other Restrictions\" paragraph of Section 6, and sits oddly with the NDA he executes simultaneously. Which warranty governs a conflict is not stated.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.10}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c033", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The parties \"consent to\" New York jurisdiction and \"stipulate that a proper and convenient venue\" is New York, without saying the forum is exclusive. Whether the clause is permissive or mandatory is a standard question of construction on these words.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c034", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c035", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This fee-shifting term makes the \"losing party\" reimburse the \"prevailing party,\" while the Remedies paragraph of Section 6 entitles the Corporation to reimbursement of all enforcement costs regardless of who prevails. Which allocation applies to a covenant suit cannot be answered from either provision alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.21}
  ]}
]}

