{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c036", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This Agreement-wide definition of \"Affiliate\" (control-based, tied to the Corporation) conflicts with the separate \"Affiliate\" definition in Section 6, which uses a ten percent ownership test and reaches Family members of any Person. The restrictive covenants use the term without saying which definition governs.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c037", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Clause (v) makes it Cause to have \"breached the Restrictive Covenants set forth in Section 5 of this Agreement,\" but Section 5 is Termination and the Restrictive Covenants are Section 6. The mis-numbered cross-reference leaves the covenant-breach trigger pointing at the wrong provision.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
    {"issue": "Clause (v) also makes any breach of \"this Agreement, or the NDA, or any material Corporation policy or other agreement\" a Cause event, a catch-all that swallows the four specific grounds enumerated before it. Whether Cause requires misconduct of the enumerated kind or any breach at all is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c038", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Disability\" turns on inability to perform essential duties \"even with reasonable accommodations,\" \"all as determined by the Board in its good faith judgment,\" with no minimum duration of incapacity specified. Because Section 5(a) makes employment terminate automatically on Disability, the absence of any time threshold or objective medical standard is consequential.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.25}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c039", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Good Reason\" is elaborately defined but the term appears nowhere else in the instrument: Section 5 gives Executive no right to resign for Good Reason and Section 4 attaches no payment to such a resignation. The definition's meaning and effect can only be assessed by reading it against a Termination section that never uses it.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.45}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c040", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This section is the one the Remedies paragraph of Section 6 invokes to create a \"Third Party Beneficiary,\" yet it confers enforcement rights only on an \"assignee or successor in interest\" and never designates a third-party beneficiary. The two provisions must be read together to know who beyond the Corporation may enforce the covenants.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c041", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The requirement that any amendment be in a signed writing sits against Section 19(b), by which the parties \"agree to work in good faith to amend this Agreement\" for Section 409A purposes. Whether that obligation can produce an amendment absent a signed writing is unresolved between the two.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c042", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This severability rule (an unenforceable covenant is simply severed) overlaps the Judicial Modification paragraph of Section 6, which requires that overbroad restrictions be \"blue penciled\" and reformed rather than struck. Which treatment a court is to apply to an overbroad restrictive covenant is left in doubt.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c043", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c044", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c045", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c046", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Law\" is defined to include only United States state and federal common law, yet the Judicial Modification paragraph of Section 6 contemplates enforcement \"under the laws of each jurisdiction in which enforcement is sought\" and the Territory covers the CIS and Europe. The definition cannot be applied to the foreign jurisdictions the covenants reach.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c047", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This definition of \"person\" enumerates a different set of entities than the capitalized \"Person\" defined in Section 6 for the Affiliate test. Which definition applies where the two lists diverge is not addressed anywhere.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c048", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c049", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Notices must be \"addressed to the addresses for the parties listed below,\" but the signature page leaves the Executive's address blank, so the clause's only address mechanism fails as to him. Whether notice to Executive can be validly given at all is a question raised by reading the section with the signature page.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c050", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Headings are declared to form no part of the Agreement, yet other provisions operate by heading — the Remedies paragraph refers to the \"Section entitled 'Third Party Enforcement; Assignment; Successors',\" and the Section 6 covenants are identified only by their headings. The disclaimer and those cross-references cannot both be given full effect.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c051", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This clause makes the Agreement effective \"as of its stated date of execution\" upon exchange of counterparts, while Section 17 makes employment under the Agreement effective on the Effective Date and Section 2 fixes that as August 15, 2014. The operative date of the instrument depends on reconciling the three.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c052", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The integration clause supersedes any \"contemporaneous agreement,\" which on its face would swallow the NDA that Section 6 says was executed \"[s]imultaneously herewith\" and that Section 9(b) makes a Cause trigger. Whether the NDA survives this clause is a direct question of the two provisions read together.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.31}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c053", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c054", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c055", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Making employment \"effective on the Effective Date\" cannot be squared with Section 14, under which the Agreement becomes effective as of its stated date of execution when counterparts are exchanged. The period between July 9 and August 15, 2014 is governed by neither provision clearly.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c056", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Survival of \"Sections 4 through 18, inclusive\" carries Section 4 (Compensation and Benefits) past termination, which cannot be squared with Section 5(b), under which all rights to salary, bonuses and benefits cease on termination. Which provision governs post-termination pay is squarely in issue.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.38}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c057", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The six-month delay operates only \"if the Corporation determines\" that Executive is a specified employee, leaving the trigger to one party's unilateral determination with no standard. Whether the delay applies at all is therefore not ascertainable from the text.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.11}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c058", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The parties merely \"agree to work in good faith to amend this Agreement\" so that it is 409A-compliant while preserving economic effect — an agreement to agree with no term specified and no fallback if they fail. What either party is bound to do cannot be determined from the words.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c059", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This acknowledgment says only that Executive \"was afforded sufficient opportunity to consult with legal counsel,\" whereas Section 7 has him represent that he \"has consulted with independent legal counsel\" regarding his rights. The two statements about the same fact are not consistent.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.14}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c060", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Exhibit A makes the Managing Director accountable for P&L and for managing \"strategic client accounts,\" which does not line up with Section 3's description of accountability for \"selected clients\" and line management of \"all personnel involved in service delivery.\" Because Exhibit A is incorporated, the actual scope of the position must be settled between the two.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.14}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c061", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The responsibilities \"include, without limitation, the following,\" so the enumerated business-development and delivery items do not bound the duties that can be assigned. What falls within the role — and therefore what a \"material reduction\" of duties under Section 9(d)(ii) would be — has no ascertainable limit.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14}
  ]}
]}

